        "problem": "Solve the inequality\n\n$$\n4x{e}^{2x}-5{e}^{2x}\\le 0.\n$$",
        "worked_solution": "First, we factor the given inequality, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x{e}^{2x}-5{e}^{2x} & \\le 0 \\\\ {e}^{2x}(4x-5) & \\le 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${e}^{2x}$ is always positive, we can divide both sides of the inequality by this quantity. By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{e}^{2x}(4x-5)}{{e}^{2x}} & \\le \\frac{0}{{e}^{2x}} \\\\ 4x-5 & \\le 0 \\\\ 4x & \\le 5 \\\\ x & \\le \\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
